From: WhaleOS <whaleos-dev@navercorp.com>
Subject: [PATCH] cras_helper_add_stream_simple: respect direction parameter

cras_helper_add_stream_simple() accepts a direction argument but
hardcodes CRAS_STREAM_OUTPUT when constructing the unified params,
making the function unable to set up capture streams.  The Android
audio HAL needs this to wire input devices through CRAS; pass the
caller-supplied direction through instead.

--- a/cras/src/libcras/cras_helpers.c
+++ b/cras/src/libcras/cras_helpers.c
@@ -133,7 +133,7 @@ int cras_helper_add_stream_simple(struct cras_client* client,
   }

   params = cras_client_unified_params_create(
-      CRAS_STREAM_OUTPUT, 2048, CRAS_STREAM_TYPE_DEFAULT, 0, user_data,
+      direction, 2048, CRAS_STREAM_TYPE_DEFAULT, 0, user_data,
       unified_cb, err_cb, aud_format);
   if (!params) {
     rc = -ENOMEM;
